{"id": "wwdc2017-813", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2017/813", "wordCount": 1389, "segments": [{"start": 21.0, "text": "In the next 10 minutes, we"}, {"start": 22.0, "text": "will learn how to use alerts to"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "make your app better, your users"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "happier, and your ratings and"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "revenues higher."}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "Good alerts can accomplish that"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "because they are one of the most"}, {"start": 34.0, "text": "efficient problem-solving tools"}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "at your disposal."}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "They help people enjoy your app,"}, {"start": 40.0, "text": "and navigate it easily, instead"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "of getting stuck in some"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "suboptimal state, getting"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "frustrated, confused, quitting"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "your app, de-installing your"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "app, and giving you one-star"}, {"start": 52.0, "text": "ratings."}, {"start": 53.0, "text": "So how do you create alerts that"}, {"start": 56.0, "text": "work?"}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "Before you get to the creating"}, {"start": 58.0, "text": "part, you should ask yourself a"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "very important question."}, {"start": 64.0, "text": "Should I be using an alert at"}, {"start": 66.0, "text": "all?"}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "Is this the best way to achieve"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "my goal?"}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "Let's look at some examples of"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "good alert use."}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "The most common one you are"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "familiar with is to correct"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "errors, like this one."}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "Alerts are also used to request"}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "access to user data, such as"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "contacts, location, or financial"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "information."}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "We provided a format for your"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "use, and put a lot of thought in"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "its content."}, {"start": 97.0, "text": "It explains concisely and"}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "clearly what data is requested,"}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "and how it will be used."}, {"start": 105.0, "text": "Alerts are also used to notify"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "people of major updates, such as"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "significant feature releases, or"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "critical security fixes."}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "These announcements should be"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "used judiciously and sparingly."}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "Reserve them only for problems"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "that merit immediate attention"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "or features that would really"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "benefit your audience, certainly"}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "not every update merits an"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "alert, and on that note, let's"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "talk about when alerts should"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "not be used."}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "I will introduce this topic with"}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "a very important point I would"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "like you to remember."}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "Alerts are disruptive by design."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "Oops, what are you doing here?"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "Can't you see I'm in the middle"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "of a talk?"}, {"start": 152.0, "text": "Don't you wish you could do this"}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "to all annoying alerts?"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "So the lesson here is, do not"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "use alerts for non-essential"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "Before putting any content in an"}, {"start": 163.0, "text": "alert, ask yourself, do people"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "really need to know this, and do"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "they need to know this now."}, {"start": 170.0, "text": "If the answer to that question"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "is not an absolute resounding"}, {"start": 174.0, "text": "yes, do not interrupt your"}, {"start": 176.0, "text": "audience."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "The next important point I would"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "like you to remember is that"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "alerts are lightweight by"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "design."}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "Their small format reflects and"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "serves the purpose of"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "facilitating quick, informed"}, {"start": 192.0, "text": "decisions, so that people can"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "make a choice, and move on with"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "whatever they were doing."}, {"start": 199.0, "text": "Therefore, do not overload"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "alerts with lengthy content, or"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "too many choices."}, {"start": 206.0, "text": "These tasks are better left to"}, {"start": 209.0, "text": "larger UI elements."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "Let's look at some examples."}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "Alerts are not settings, nor are"}, {"start": 217.0, "text": "they multiple choice questions."}, {"start": 219.0, "text": "You can see that the actions are"}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "struggling to fit into the"}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "provided format, and here is a"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "hint for you."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "If your alert takes most of the"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "supported view port, it is time"}, {"start": 231.0, "text": "to cut down or relegate some of"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "the tasks to larger elements."}, {"start": 238.0, "text": "Alerts are full-scale diagnostic"}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "tools."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "Do not use them to expose"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "technical data, especially error"}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "codes."}, {"start": 249.0, "text": "Alerts are not afterthoughts."}, {"start": 251.0, "text": "Do not use them to fix"}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "preventable problems."}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "For example, if you have"}, {"start": 256.0, "text": "password rules, articulate them"}, {"start": 259.0, "text": "clearly on the main screen."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "You can also disallow invalid"}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "character input."}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "However, the thing to not do is"}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "to make users memorize a long,"}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "complicated list of characters,"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "and then go back to fix the"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "problem that should not have"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "occurred in the first place."}, {"start": 280.0, "text": "To summarize, the dos and don'ts"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "of alerts, use them to correct"}, {"start": 284.0, "text": "errors, request access to"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "customer data, or notify people"}, {"start": 289.0, "text": "of major updates."}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "Do not use them for"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "non-essential or lengthy"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "content."}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "Do not offer complicated"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "choices."}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "And do not duplicate the tasks"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "of other UI elements."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "Now, you have considered all"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "these factors and decided that"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "you need an alert after all."}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "So how do you go about writing a"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "successful one?"}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "It turns out that the structure"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "of the alert, with its clear"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "separation of visual elements"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "already sets you on this path of"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "success."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "Let's go back to our good alert"}, {"start": 326.0, "text": "example, and see how we can make"}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "use of that structure."}, {"start": 330.0, "text": "In the title, state your main"}, {"start": 334.0, "text": "point in one sentence or less."}, {"start": 339.0, "text": "In the message details, provide"}, {"start": 341.0, "text": "brief additional information if"}, {"start": 343.0, "text": "necessary, such as the cause of"}, {"start": 345.0, "text": "the error, or the reason for"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "your request."}, {"start": 350.0, "text": "Offer actions that are easy to"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "understand and perform."}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "If you have to take people"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "outside the app, or to a"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "different state, make sure to"}, {"start": 360.0, "text": "navigate them there."}, {"start": 362.0, "text": "Do not leave this job to the"}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "Back button, the Home button,"}, {"start": 365.0, "text": "the main screen, or otherwise"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "leave users to find their way."}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "If people scan the title and the"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "actions, ideally, they should be"}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "able to understand what is going"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "on without paying too much"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "attention to the message"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "details."}, {"start": 381.0, "text": "While this is not always"}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "possible, it is a good goal to"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "aspire to."}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "And if you need a quick mnemonic"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "rule, a good alert answers three"}, {"start": 391.0, "text": "key questions."}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "What happened?"}, {"start": 394.0, "text": "Why people are seeing this?"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "And how this should proceed"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "based on the information they've"}, {"start": 400.0, "text": "received."}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "Now that you've mastered the"}, {"start": 403.0, "text": "structure of the alert, let's"}, {"start": 405.0, "text": "practice and apply these"}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "guidelines to fix some common"}, {"start": 409.0, "text": "problems."}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "Let's read through this one."}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "\"App name\" cannot open this"}, {"start": 415.0, "text": "file."}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "The title is accurate, but not"}, {"start": 418.0, "text": "especially helpful."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "Which file do we mean?"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "People may be working with"}, {"start": 423.0, "text": "multiple files."}, {"start": 425.0, "text": "You may need to download the"}, {"start": 427.0, "text": "latest available updates for the"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "app. Do you want to visit the \"app"}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "name\" website for more"}, {"start": 432.0, "text": "information and troubleshooting"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "tips?"}, {"start": 435.0, "text": "These instructions are vague and"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "tentative, and suggest multiple"}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "outcomes, and that is also a lot"}, {"start": 440.0, "text": "of text."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "No. Yes. The actions are"}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "difficult to understand without"}, {"start": 448.0, "text": "going back and reading said"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "lengthy instructions."}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "Let's see how we can improve"}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "this."}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "First, let's specify the file"}, {"start": 457.0, "text": "name for clarity."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "Next, let's pare down the"}, {"start": 463.0, "text": "instructions for simplicity."}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "Finally, let's offer clear"}, {"start": 469.0, "text": "actionable choices, so that"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "people understand what happens"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "when they tap on any one of"}, {"start": 474.0, "text": "them."}, {"start": 476.0, "text": "Here is your before and after."}, {"start": 478.0, "text": "Which one do you think looks"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "better?"}, {"start": 482.0, "text": "Thought so."}, {"start": 484.0, "text": "Now, let's take a look at an"}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "alert that seems to be written"}, {"start": 488.0, "text": "with all the guidelines in mind."}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "Let's read through this one."}, {"start": 494.0, "text": "Cancel download?"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "If you cancel now, you will not"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "receive this file."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "Cancel? Okay ."}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "There is nothing wrong with any"}, {"start": 505.0, "text": "individual part, the title"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "states the question, the message"}, {"start": 510.0, "text": "describes the consequences, and"}, {"start": 513.0, "text": "even the actions use the"}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "recommended terminology."}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "Cancel and okay."}, {"start": 519.0, "text": "However, this is a classic"}, {"start": 521.0, "text": "example of a confusing alert"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "that happens even to the most"}, {"start": 525.0, "text": "experienced developers."}, {"start": 527.0, "text": "So the lesson here is, even when"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "using guidelines, always check"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "the result for any ambiguity or"}, {"start": 535.0, "text": "confusion."}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "Let's see how we can clarify"}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "this one."}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "First, let's rephrase the title"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "to remove ambiguity and mention"}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "the filename to be more"}, {"start": 546.0, "text": "specific."}, {"start": 549.0, "text": "Next, let's apply similar"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "changes to the message details."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "And for good measure, let's"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "reiterate the choices and the"}, {"start": 557.0, "text": "actions, so people understand"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "what happens if they click on"}, {"start": 561.0, "text": "any of them."}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "Here is your before and after."}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "And I hope you would agree that"}, {"start": 568.0, "text": "the after looks a bit better"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "than the before."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "Now, you have learned how to"}, {"start": 574.0, "text": "make use of the structure, let's"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "talk a bit about style and"}, {"start": 578.0, "text": "quality."}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "Here, I have a couple of tips"}, {"start": 583.0, "text": "for you."}, {"start": 584.0, "text": "Avoid platitudes, jargon or"}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "fillers."}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "All they do is take space"}, {"start": 588.0, "text": "without adding any return value."}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "Use correct formatting,"}, {"start": 594.0, "text": "spelling, and punctuation."}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "This seems like a very basic"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "piece of advice, but it will go"}, {"start": 600.0, "text": "a very long way toward making"}, {"start": 602.0, "text": "your alerts and your app look"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "polished and professional."}, {"start": 607.0, "text": "Finally, consider your audience."}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "Whether you are writing for"}, {"start": 611.0, "text": "medical professionals, special"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "needs students, or even a very"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "smart cat who just learned how"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "to use an iPad, make sure that"}, {"start": 619.0, "text": "your editorial voice matches"}, {"start": 621.0, "text": "their needs and expectations."}, {"start": 625.0, "text": "In conclusion, here are the"}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "three simple things you can do"}, {"start": 628.0, "text": "now to make your alerts awesome."}, {"start": 633.0, "text": "Keep them simple and helpful."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "Go practice."}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "Take what you learned, go"}, {"start": 639.0, "text": "through your app, see if you"}, {"start": 641.0, "text": "need all the alerts that you"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "created, and if you do, see how"}, {"start": 645.0, "text": "you can make them work harder."}, {"start": 648.0, "text": "And for more information and an"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "in-depth look on how to write"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "alerts for iOS and macOS, read"}, {"start": 655.0, "text": "the HIG available at the Apple"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "website."}]}